{"step_index":109,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:52:39Z","thinking":"**Reviewing request and feedback**\n\nReviewing the user's request is paramount before proceeding. The request specifies using a configuration file for a handoff review. Need to prioritize onboarding improvements by analyzing feedback on status filters and digest quietness.\n\n\n**Analyzing weekly feedback reports**\n\nThe weekly feedback includes two specific items: the lack of status filters on the mobile app and the persistent evening pings from the \"quiet digest.\" The mobile filter feedback is related to a solo owner on Android 15. The quiet digest feedback comes from a contributor in a large EU team.\n\nI am thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n**Reconciling user feedback with known states**\n\nThe user's mobile status filter feedback indicates a regression or unmet need despite the prior \"Focus Shelf\" initiative, which was supposedly shelved due to low use. The handoff notes a conflicting claim, requiring a review of past actions and assumptions about the \"Focus Shelf\" feature. It seems that \"Focus Shelf\" is the feature that is related to the status filters; the user is requesting something that the archived feature has.\n\n\n**Investigating prior feature deployment**\n\nThe \"Focus Shelf\" feature, related to status filters, was initially deployed to desktop enterprise accounts only (May 14).  Low reported usage (2%) led to a rollback, but this was due to incorrect denominator including automation accounts and slow count queries for large workspaces. A later release (August 30) addressed the performance issue by making count queries asynchronous and deploying the status filters to all desktop accounts. The mobile component remains a draft.\n\n\n**Confirming mobile feature status**\n\nReviewing additional records confirms that mobile clients lack status filter controls, matching the user's feedback. Evidence from September 6th explicitly states the absence of mobile support. The mobile component is still a draft, according to a separate record, explaining the lack of filter functionality on the user's Android 15 device.\n\n\n**Investigating \"quiet digest\" issue**\n\nThe \"Sunday Room\" feature, also known as \"quiet digest,\" was deployed on July 12 and allowed workspace administrators to choose weekly digests instead of daily. This change did not migrate contributor-level legacy daily subscriptions. Evidence shows a support ticket indicating a contributor continues to receive daily pings, confirming the migration limitation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 /workspace/skill/scripts/history.py search /workspace/product \\\"onboarding\\\" --limit 10\"","Cwd":"\"/workspace\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Search for onboarding in product history\""}}]}
