{"step_index":115,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:52:51Z","thinking":"**Reviewing Long-Horizon Skill Details**\n\nInitial focus on using specified data for the handoff review. Determine if \"status filters on phone\" and \"quieter digest\" are viable improvements for this week. Need to examine past attempts, outcomes, and next steps for both suggestions within the product context.\n\n\n**Evaluating Onboarding Improvements**\n\nInitial assessment suggests no specific week is identified for the onboarding improvements, but \"status filters on phone\" and \"quieter digest\" are viable candidates. Checking for prior actions and outcomes related to these improvement ideas in the available records, to assess their historical context and feasibility for next steps. Determining how previous attempts were terminated will inform whether to consider them again.\n\n\n**Examining Mobile Status Filters**\n\nPast attempts at status filters (Focus Shelf) were restricted to desktop and encountered performance issues on large workspaces. The original usage report incorrectly included automation accounts, skewing the usage data. Evaluating if the performance issues are resolvable, as mobile was excluded from the previous experiment.\n\n**Considering Digest Quieter Options**\n\nThe second feedback item pertains to a \"quieter digest\". No specific prior action on this topic exists in the records. Determining the exact meaning of \"quieter\" in this context is the first priority.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Desktop Feature Outcomes**\n\nThe August release included an architectural fix that resolved desktop performance bottlenecks. The September activity report revision shows 21% human weekly usage, debunking a \"low use\" misconception. This usage data needs to be considered in conjunction with prior mobile status information which explicitly states no mobile availability.\n\n**Analyzing \"Quieter Digest\" Feedback**\n\nFeedback suggests a user needs only a weekly digest instead of the current frequency. The \"age_days=20\" value in the feedback record is misleading, representing days since the digest release, not ticket submission date. Further refin\n<truncated 700 bytes>\nibility's scope without owner approval.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Status Filters**\n\nMobile status filters offer the most direct path to reduce onboarding friction based on observed problems. This addresses a specific user pain point where they must scroll through long task lists. The desktop version's proven success, existing mobile component, and resolved performance bottlenecks ensure a high probability of a positive outcome.\n\n**Confirming Digest Limitations**\n\nThe limitations on the \"quieter digest\" feedback make it less actionable, as the legacy daily subscription issue would require restarting a terminated system. Mobile status filters are a concrete solution, with demonstrated desktop success. Therefore it's preferable to address this.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Filter Component**\n\nThe \"quieter digest\" is not the immediate priority, because its underlying notification-reset component has been terminated. Resurrecting this feature is outside the scope of the current work. Furthermore, the ticket's age is uncertain.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n**Recommending Mobile Status Filter Deployment**\n\nThe existing mobile component for status filters shows a path to reduce onboarding friction; desktop status filters now have solved performance bottlenecks (`current.md`). Desktop usage shows a 21% human weekly usage rate. The mobile implementation for status filter is the next logical step to replicate success.\n\nInvestigating `history/support/record-0131162d69.md` revealed initial performance issues for the Focus Shelf feature, but the architectural fix from August addressed the performance bottlenecks. The \"quieter digest\" feedback is less actionable, given the limitations in legacy subscriptions.\n\nDeployment for this week can begin, given the existing mobile component. The uncertainty lies in mobile performance on larger workspaces, mobile draft component readiness/testing across iOS/Android, and also the unknown submission date of ticket `record-5f1a34c149`.\n\nRecommend mobile status filter deployment.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"grep -E \\\"(Submitted|Retrieved|Dated):\\\" /workspace/product/history/support/*.md\"","Cwd":"\"/workspace\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Check dates in all history/support files\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
