{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:53:08Z","thinking":"**Formulating Initial Recommendation**\n\nThe instruction requires a dated recommendation, including prior actions, evidence-based support, a next action, and uncertainty. A `/workspace/work/decision.md` file should be created. I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Onboarding Improvements**\n\nThe provided information establishes the current date as 2026-09-08 and directs the focus to reducing onboarding friction. User feedback highlights desired status filters on mobile and quieter digest options. The `/workspace/skill/SKILL.md` file needs examination for context on long-term goals. The goal is to identify actions taken, results, and propose the next improvement.\n\n\n**Reviewing Past Product Decisions**\n\nThe `/workspace/product/current.md` file, dated 2026-08-20, identifies shelved features and a shipped digest. The file highlights the need to keep the next objective small. The history/support directory contains the current week's feedback export, which will inform this effort.\n\nThe `SKILL.md` file contains guidelines regarding historical record usage, and the distinction between event/deployment/observation timelines. Past failures are noted as potential future opportunities given changing conditions. The notification reset responsibility is identified, but will not be resumed.\n\n\n**Assessing Feature Rollout History**\n\nExamining the feedback indicates a user need for status filters on mobile, mirroring desktop functionality. The \"Focus Shelf,\" previously shelved, initially included only desktop accounts, suggesting that the mobile platforms were excluded. A rollout was attempted but was rolled back due to performance issues.\n\nFurther investigation is required to determine the current state of the \"Focus Shelf\" and feasibility of re-introducing it with a platform expansion. It’s also necessary to analyze why mobile was excluded initially and whether the performance bottleneck has been addressed. The `/workspace/work/decision.md` file will log these insights.\n\n\n**Evaluating Mobile Feature Rollout\n<truncated 2227 bytes>\nmobile draft component and verify it uses asynchronous queries.\n\n\n**Planning Mobile Filter Implementation**\n\nMobile smoke tests are required on Android 15 and iOS with small to medium task lists, reflecting the scope of ticket `record-e36f0fe1aa`. A reversible rollout plan needs to be prepared within current authority.\n\n**Addressing Digest Issue Documentation**\n\nThe digest issue finding needs documentation for future consideration by the product lead. This documentation will highlight the cause, which involves legacy subscriptions under `record-8f6b82ec51`. The issue will be excluded from this onboarding sprint.\n\n**Assessing Implementation Uncertainties**\n\nMobile performance on larger workspaces presents an unknown, as only small workspace desktop checks passed. Component completeness and platform parity between Android and iOS is unclear, especially regarding `record-b9a1361197.md`.\nThe daily digest noise is uncertain regarding the severity/scope of the issue; submission date of ticket `record-5f1a34c149` is also unknown.\n\n\n**Confirming Recommendation Details**\n\nThe decision date is 2026-09-09, derived from the current local time and brief review. File `/workspace/work/decision.md` will structure and record the product recommendation. The recommendation scope will include details on status filters on mobile.\n\n**Specifying Implementation Details**\n\nThe implementation is under weekly-product responsibility (Sam, product lead). The brief is dated 2026-09-08 and details the reduction of onboarding friction on mobile and desktop. The core recommendation is to advance mobile status filters (draft) over the quieter digest.\n\n**Organizing Decision Documentation**\n\nThe decision document will have a date of 2026-09-09, and inclu