{"step_index":125,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:53:50Z","content":"I have completed the handoff review following the `$long-horizon` skill guidelines and saved the dated recommendation to [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings & Decision\n\n* **Selected Improvement:** **Mobile Status Filters** (advancing the draft mobile component to verification and an initial reversible pilot on Android).\n* **What We Already Tried vs. What Actually Happened:**\n  * **Status Filters / \"Focus Shelf\":** Contrary to the stale handoff note in [`current.md`](file:///workspace/product/current.md#L2), the feature was not abandoned due to lack of interest. The initial 2% usage rate ([`record-8a2203deaa.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-8a2203deaa.md#L2-L4)) was diluted by bot accounts, and its June 2 rollback ([`record-ecc0d14c71.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-ecc0d14c71.md#L2-L4)) was caused by slow synchronous count queries. On August 30, asynchronous count queries were deployed to all desktop accounts ([`record-b9a1361197.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md#L2)), achieving **21% human weekly usage** ([`record-dfcc7fb912.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-dfcc7fb912.md#L2)). However, mobile was omitted and remained a draft component. Ticket [`record-e36f0fe1aa`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md#L2) (submitted 2026-09-05) demonstrates that new solo owners on Android 15 encounter immediate onboarding friction without it.\n  * **Quieter Digest / \"Sunday Room\":** While [`record-8f6b82ec51.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/notification-reset/actions/record-8f6b82ec51.md#L2) shipped on July 12, it only allowed workspace *administrators* to select weekly team digests; contributor-level legacy daily subscriptions were **not** migrated. While this explains why ticket [`record-5f1a34c149`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-0131162d69.md#L3) still receives daily emails, its submission date is **unknown** (`age_days=20` is days since release, not ticket age), it concerns existing enterprise team contributors rather than onboarding friction, and the originating responsibility `notification-reset` terminated on July 31 ([`notification-reset/brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/notification-reset/brief.md#L2)), placing email preference migration outside our standing weekly onboarding remit.\n* **Next Useful Action This Week:** Inspect the draft mobile filter component, confirm it integrates with the asynchronous backend endpoints from [`record-40440b02ae`](file:///workspace/product/history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md#L2), execute smoke checks on mobile for small task lists (matching the 34-task cohort in ticket `record-e36f0fe1aa`), and prepare a reversible rollout specification.\n\nFor the complete analysis, evidence breakdowns, and citation ledger, please inspect [decision.md](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).","thinking":"**Reviewing Handoff and Feedback**\n\nReviewing the user request again confirms the core tasks: incorporate `long-horizon` from the specified skill file for handoff, address onboarding feedback, and use the product workspace for context. The onboarding improvements focus on status filters for mobile and a quieter digest. Understanding past attempts and outcomes for each improvement is the next step.\n\n\n"}
